# ===========================================================================
# Frontend ignore rules
# ===========================================================================
#
# Scaffolded by `npm create vite`. The repository root has its own
# .gitignore covering secrets and build output for both halves of the
# project; this file only adds the Vite- and editor-specific entries.
#
# Patterns without a leading slash match at any depth, so `node_modules`
# below also covers a nested one.
# ===========================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Package managers write crash reports into the working directory. They are
# machine-specific and useless to anyone else.
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies and build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# node_modules is reinstalled from package-lock.json by `npm ci`.
node_modules
# `vite build` output, deployed by Vercel and regenerated every time.
dist
# Server-side render bundle. Unused here, but Vite emits it if SSR is on.
dist-ssr
# Vite's convention for machine-local overrides — .env.local, and anything
# else a developer wants kept off the branch.
*.local

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor and OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ignore VS Code settings, but keep extensions.json so a new developer is
# still prompted to install the extensions this project expects.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
# macOS Finder metadata. Several are already tracked from before this rule
# existed; `git rm --cached` would be needed to drop them.
.DS_Store
# Visual Studio solution and project files.
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
# Vim swap files (.swp, .swo).
*.sw?
